{"created": "2024-08-02T11:52:49.811060+00:00", "modified": "2024-08-02T11:52:50.189396+00:00", "id": 13168643, "conceptrecid": "6610488", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6610488", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "metadata": {"title": "AIT Netflow Data Set", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "publication_date": "2024-08-02", "description": "<p><strong>AIT Netflow Data Sets</strong></p>\n<p>This repository contains labeled synthetic netflows suitable for evaluation of intrusion detection systems, federated learning, and alert aggregation. The netflows are generated from the packet captures contained in the <a href=\"http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5789064\">AIT-LDS-v2.0</a>. A detailed description of that dataset is available in [1]. The packet captures were collected from eight testbeds that were built at the Austrian Institute of Technology (AIT) following the approach by [2]. Please cite these papers if the data is used for academic publications.</p>\n<p>In brief, each of the datasets corresponds to a testbed representing a small enterprise network including mail server, file share, WordPress server, VPN, firewall, etc. Normal user behavior is simulated to generate background noise over a time span of 4-6 days. At some point, a sequence of attack steps is launched against the network. The following attacks are launched in the network:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scans (nmap, WPScan, dirb)</li>\n<li>Webshell upload (CVE-2020-24186)</li>\n<li>Password cracking (John the Ripper)</li>\n<li>Privilege escalation</li>\n<li>Remote command execution</li>\n<li>Data exfiltration (DNSteal)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This repository contains the following files:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>&lt;testbed&gt;_netflows.zip</em>: CSV files of labeled TCP and UDP netflows for each testbed.</li>\n<li><em>label_info.txt</em>: File describing which labels in TCP and UDP are benign and which ones are malicious.</li>\n<li><em>README.md</em>: Instructions on how to reproduce the generation and labeling of the netflows from the <a href=\"http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5789064\">AIT-LDS-v2.0</a>. Note that it is only necessary to run the python scripts if you want to extend or change the labeling procedure.</li>\n<li><em>1_format_dataset_info.ipynb</em>: Generates the tables necessary for labeling (see README.md).</li>\n<li><em>2_label_logs.ipynb</em>: Labels the netflows (see README.md).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Acknowledgements: Partially funded by the FFG projects INDICAETING (868306) and DECEPT (873980), and the EU projects GUARD (833456) and PANDORA (SI2.835928).</p>\n<p><strong>If you use the dataset, please cite the following publications:</strong></p>\n<p>[1] M. Landauer, F. Skopik, M. Frank, W. Hotwagner, M. Wurzenberger, and A. Rauber. <a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/9866880\">\"Maintainable Log Datasets for Evaluation of Intrusion Detection Systems\"</a>. IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing, vol. 20, no. 4, pp. 3466-3482. [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.08580.pdf\">PDF</a>]</p>\n<p>[2]&nbsp;M. Landauer, F. Skopik, M. Wurzenberger, W. Hotwagner and A. Rauber, <a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9262078\">\"Have it Your Way: Generating Customized Log Datasets With a Model-Driven Simulation Testbed,\"</a> in IEEE Transactions on Reliability, vol. 70, no. 1, pp. 402-415, March 2021, doi: 10.1109/TR.2020.3031317. [<a href=\"https://www.skopik.at/ait/2020_trel.pdf\">PDF</a>]</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Soro, Francesca", "affiliation": "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Landauer, Max", "affiliation": "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Skopik, Florian", "affiliation": "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Hotwagner, Wolfgang", "affiliation": "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Wurzenberger, Markus", "affiliation": "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"}], "keywords": ["netflows", "intrusion detection"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "833456", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100000780::833456", "funder": {"name": "European Commission", "doi": "10.13039/501100000780", "acronym": "EC"}, "title": "A cybersecurity framework to GUArantee Reliability and trust for Digital service chains", "acronym": "GUARD", "program": "H2020-EU.2.1.1.", "url": "https://cordis.europa.eu/projects/833456"}], "communities": [{"id": "eu"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6610488"}}]}, "notes": "M. Landauer, F. Skopik, M. Frank, W. Hotwagner, M. Wurzenberger, and A. Rauber. \"Maintainable Log Datasets for Evaluation of Intrusion Detection Systems\". IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing, vol. 20, no. 4, pp. 3466-3482."}, "title": "AIT Netflow Data Set", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13168643", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13168643?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.13168643", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6610488", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6610488", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6610488", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6610488", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:13168643/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:13168643/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13168643/media-files-archive", "lates